# Every image builds with the repo root as its context (the uv lockfile is
# workspace-wide), so without this the whole checkout is sent to the builder.
#
# node_modules is the one that breaks things rather than just slowing them:
# docker/frontend/Dockerfile runs `npm install` and then `COPY src/frontend/`,
# which would lay the host's node_modules — macOS binaries for esbuild and
# rollup — over the Linux ones it just installed.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.venv
.git
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.claude
docs
tests

# Never send local secrets into a build context.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
